What is HoneyPot:

Honeypot ek jaal (trap) system hota hai. Yeh jaanbujhkar ek asli device jaisa dikhta hai (Windows XP, Apache server, Router, Printer),
lekin isme koi real data ya real kaam nahi hota. Iska maqsad hai attackers ko attract karna aur unki activity record karna.


=> Kaam kaise karta hai

Honeypot ek fake service chalata hai, jaise SSH (port 22), Telnet (23), HTTP (80), SMB (445).
Attacker ko lagta hai yeh asli, vulnerable machine hai.
Wo scan karta hai, login try karta hai, exploit chalata hai.
Honeypot sab log karta hai: attacker ka IP, username/password, commands, malware, exploit payload.
Asli system ko koi nuksan nahi hota, kyunki yeh sab isolated hai.

=> Example:
python3 main.py device:web:windows:windowsxp nccc 3 ek Windows XP device ka fake profile chalata hai.

1. Honeypot - Decoder compiling: 
matlab yeh attack patterns pehchanne wale decoders load kar raha hai: CVE exploits (Fortinet, Cisco, Struts, PHP), XOR shellcode, base64 payloads, Metasploit patterns.
2. Capture_Packet_started = network traffic capture ho raha hai.
3. Event Manager Started = attack events ko record aur alert karega.
4. Port Scanner Started = port scan detect karega.


. TIA table me alag-alag profiles hain (windowsxp, apache-server, checkpoint firewall, Cisco router, HPLaserJet printer, Openhab). Yeh sab alag-alag fake devices hain jo Power sector testbed ki DMZ me lage hain,
taaki attackers ICS/power infrastructure jaisa target samjhein.

. smb folder ke andar reverse_fake_shell.py, smb32.py, smbetx64.py jaise files hain. Yeh SMB exploits (jaise EternalBlue type) ko emulate karti hain, aur fake shell dikhati hain taaki attacker aage commands chalaye aur uska behaviour record ho.



. Honeypot kyun use karte hain

Naye attacks aur zero-day ka pata chalta hai.
Attacker ke tools aur TTPs (tactics, techniques, procedures) samajh aate hain.
Threat intelligence milti hai: malicious IPs, malware samples.
Early warning system ki tarah kaam karta hai. Honeypot par koi bhi connection suspicious hota hai, kyunki koi legitimate user ise use nahi karta.

. Types

Low-interaction: sirf basic services emulate karta hai (zyada safe, kam detail).
High-interaction: asli OS/service deta hai (zyada detail, zyada risk).
Medium-interaction: aapka jaisa lagta hai, jo fake shell aur protocols emulate karta hai.


==> Honeypot real machine se network ke through connect hota hai. Yeh ek alag IP address leta hai aur network par ek aur device ki tarah dikhta hai. Real machine se connect karne ke 3 tarike hain.

1. Docker port mapping (aapka abhi ka setup)
  Container ke andar ki service ko host machine ke port se jod dete hain:
  docker run -it -p 2222:22 -p 8080:80 -p 2323:23 <image>
 Note: 
  2222:22 matlab host ka port 2222 → container ka SSH port 22
  Koi bhi HOST-IP:2222 par connect karega, to honeypot jawab dega.

2. Alag IP dena (macvlan network), production jaisa
 Jaisa  TIA table me hai (117.254.54.69, .68, .67...), har honeypot ka apna IP hota hai. Isme Docker container ko LAN par seedha ek alag IP milta hai:

docker network create -d macvlan \
  --subnet=117.254.54.0/24 --gateway=117.254.54.1 \
  -o parent=eth0 hp_net

Is tarah attacker ko lagta hai ki woh ek alag physical device hai. (Subnet aur gateway apne network ke hisaab se badlein.)

3. Host network mode
  docker run -it --network host <image>


Container host ka hi IP aur ports use karta hai. Simple hai, lekin real services ke ports se conflict ho sakta hai (jaise host par asli SSH 22 pe chal raha ho).

Real machine ko honeypot se kaise jodte hain

Attacker/tester machine (alag PC ya Kali): nmap -sV 117.254.54.69 ya ssh user@117.254.54.69 karke dekhiye. Honeypot ke terminal me events aayenge.
Dashboard (TIA): honeypot ke events central server tak jaate hain. Isliye “Device Registration” me device register hota hai (IP, TIA profile, zone). network_config.json aur config folder me server ka address aur settings hoti hain.
DMZ me lagana: honeypot ko DMZ zone me rakhte hain (jaisa aapke table me hai), taaki internet/external traffic isse mile, lekin internal network tak na pahunche.

Security ka dhyan

Honeypot ko real production network se isolate rakhein (VLAN ya firewall rules).
Honeypot ke andar se outbound traffic restrict karein, warna compromise hone par attacker doosre systems par jaa sakta hai.
Real SSH/admin access alag port ya management network (MGMT zone) par rakhein.
Honeypot me koi real credential ya real data na rakhein.

Aapke case me

Aap abhi Docker Desktop (Windows) par test kar rahe hain, to port mapping (tarika 1) sabse aasaan hai. Macvlan Windows Docker Desktop par theek se kaam nahi karta, woh Linux (Ubuntu) machine par use hota hai. 
Aapke Ubuntu lab machine par tarika 2 chalega.

Agar aap bataein ki aapka network layout kya hai (kitne IP milte hain, VLAN hai ya nahi), to main exact docker network create command bana deta hoon.


===> Services Means honeypot ke andar kaun-kaun si network services (programs jo kisi port par sunte hain) chalu hongi, jinse attacker connect kar sake.

Simple example

Ek asli server me alag-alag darwaze (ports) hote hain. Har darwaze par ek service baithi hoti hai:

Service	                                         Port                                  	Attacker kya karta hai

SSH	                                              22	                            Remote login, password guess (brute force)
Telnet	                                          23	                            Purana remote login, IoT devices par common attack
HTTP / Web                                       	80	                            Website par exploit, path traversal
SMB                                             	445	                            Windows file sharing, EternalBlue jaise exploits


Kyun zaroori hai

Realistic dikhne ke liye: Windows XP honeypot me SMB (445) hona chahiye, warna attacker ko shak hoga. Printer me Telnet/HTTP hota hai, SSH nahi.
Attack attract karne ke liye: jo service vulnerable version ke saath khuli hogi (jaise Apache 2.4.49), us par attack aayenge.
Risk kam rakhne ke liye: jitni kam services, utna chhota attack surface.






















